{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 17, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. the movie begins with mark zuckerberg, played by jesse eisenberg, as a harvard undergraduate who is trying to find his place in the world. after being dumped by his girlfriend, erica, mark creates a website called facemash, which compares the photos of two students and asks users to vote on which one is more attractive.\n\nthe site becomes incredibly popular, but also generates a lot of controversy and gets mark into trouble with the university. however, it also catches the attention of cameron and tyler winklevoss, two wealthy and popular harvard students who approach mark with an idea for a social networking site exclusively for harvard students.\n\nmark agrees to work on the site, but soon becomes obsessed with the project and begins to neglect his relationships with his friends and family. he also meets sean parker, the co-founder of napster, who becomes a mentor and friend to mark. sean's character is played by justin timberlake, who brings a lot of energy and charisma to the role.\n\nas the site, which is initially called \"thefacebook,\" begins to gain popularity, mark and his friends become embroiled in a series of lawsuits and power struggles. the winklevoss twins claim that mark stole their idea, while mark's friend and co-founder, eduardo saverin, becomes increasingly frustrated with mark's behavior and the direction of the company.\n\nthe film is directed by david fincher, who is known for his dark and atmospheric style. he does a great job of capturing the mood and tone of the film, which is often tense and unsettling. the cinematography is also excellent, with a lot of close-ups and handheld camera work that adds to the sense of intimacy and realism.\n\nthe script, which was written by aaron sorkin, is also excellent. it's witty and engaging, with a lot of clever dialogue and interesting characters. the film is based on a book called \"the accidental billionaires,\" which tells the story of the founding of facebook. however, the film takes some creative liberties with the story, and it's not entirely clear what's fact and what's fiction.\n\noverall, the social network is a great film that explores the complexities and challenges of creating a successful startup. it's a fascinating story that's full of interesting characters and plot twists, and it's also a great commentary on the consequences of success and the importance of relationships and ethics in business. the film features a lot of strong performances, particularly from jesse eisenberg and justin timberlake, and it's a must-see for anyone who's interested in technology, entrepreneurship, or social media.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.0032289293594658375}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.04858766868710518}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.00862350407987833}, {"token": " a", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.16893017292022705}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.000523430178873241}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -0.4065585434436798}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.006261374801397324}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -0.026508038863539696}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -5.960462772236497e-07}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -0.0001209901092806831}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.4740769863128662}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -5.960462772236497e-07}, {"token": " subsequent", "logprob": -0.5213401913642883}, {"token": " lawsuits", "logprob": -0.3690207004547119}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -7.867782187531702e-06}, {"token": " followed", "logprob": -0.0010701649589464068}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -4.887569048150908e-06}, {